  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\n**Logic: (a, b, c) **→ (a × 3) + 7 = b and c = b + 4\n\n(5, 22, 26) → (5 × 3) + 7 = 15 + 7 = 22 and 26 = 22 + 4\n\n(11, 40, 44) → (11 × 3) + 7 = 33 + 7 = 40 and 44 = 40 + 4\n\nLet's check each option:\n\n1. (16, 66, 70) → (16 × 3) + 7 = 48 + 7 = 55 ≠ 66 and 70 = 66 + 4\n\n2. (17, 58, 54) → (17 × 3) + 7 = 51 + 7 = 58 but 54 ≠ 58 + 4 = 62\n\n3. (16, 55, 59) → (16 × 3) + 7 = 48 + 7 = 55 and 59 = 55 + 4 \n\n4. (13, 32, 36) → (13 × 3) + 7 = 39 + 7 = 46 ≠ 32 and 36 = 32 + 4\n\nThus, (16, 55, 59) is the set in which the numbers are related in the same way as the given sets.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"**Option 3**\".",
